celld-ml is an OCaml reimplementation of the architecture of celld
(https://github.com/denoland/celld), Copyright 2026 Deno Land Inc.,
licensed under the Apache License 2.0. lib/ltx follows celld's LTX
format and crates/ltx and was rewritten in OCaml; the protocols in
lib/logic, lib/wire and unikernels/node follow celld's design. These are
modified works: none of celld's source is included verbatim.

scripts/fetch-vendor.sh downloads the SQLite 3.54.1 amalgamation
(https://sqlite.org), which is in the public domain, into lib/sqlite.

It also downloads the QuickJS engine, release 2026-06-04
(https://bellard.org/quickjs), Copyright (c) 2017-2021 Fabrice Bellard and
Charlie Gordon, under the MIT License, into lib/js/quickjs (its LICENSE
comes with it), and modifies one line of quickjs.c, marked "celld-ml", so
Atomics can be turned off with CELLD_NO_ATOMICS. Built unikernels contain
both, so distributing them carries these notices.
